# Backtesting UI Fix - March 7, 2026

## Issue
Backtesting was completing successfully on the backend (557 trades, +52.52% return) but the frontend was showing an infinite spinner and not displaying results.

## Root Cause
The polling logic had a fatal flaw: **any network error would immediately stop polling**. The catch block called `clearInterval(poll)` on the first error, preventing the frontend from ever seeing completed results.

## Fixes Applied

### 1. Robust Polling Logic (`Backtesting.js`)
**Before:**
```javascript
catch (err) {
  clearInterval(poll);  // ❌ STOPS on first error
  setError('Failed to check status');
  setLoading(false);
}
```

**After:**
```javascript
catch (err) {
  console.error('[Backtesting] Polling error:', err);
  // ✅ Continue polling on network errors, only stop on timeout
  if (attempts >= maxAttempts) {
    clearInterval(poll);
    setError(`Failed to check status: ${err.message}`);
    setLoading(false);
  }
}
```

### 2. Better Error Handling
- Added HTTP status code checks before parsing JSON
- Added detailed console logging for debugging
- Network errors no longer stop polling immediately
- Only timeout (60 attempts = 5 minutes) stops polling

### 3. Enhanced User Feedback

#### Success Banner
When results load, shows:
```
✅ Backtest Complete!
Analyzed 557 trades with 56.2% win rate
```

#### Loading Indicator
Added animated progress bar:
```
🚀 Backtest Running...
Analyzing historical data and simulating trades. This usually takes 1-2 minutes.
[========================================70%]
```

### 4. Improved Console Logging
Added debug logs to track:
- Poll attempts and status
- Results received
- Success/failure state
- HTTP response codes

